  "annotations": [
    { "id": "note-redesign", "page": "page-redesign", "x": 0, "y": -220, "w": 560, "text": "Three modern directions for the team to choose from — each shown on the two screens that matter most (Ship, and the landing hero). Same product, same copy; only the visual system changes.\n\nPick one and the whole app gets re-skinned to it: tokens, fonts, buttons, inputs, nav, cards. Mix is fine too (\"Studio layout, Sunny colours\")." },
    { "id": "note-studio", "page": "page-redesign", "x": 3080, "y": 0, "w": 340, "text": "STUDIO — clean SaaS\n\nPlus Jakarta Sans · light neutrals · indigo accent · 12–14px radii · soft shadows · sidebar navigation · rates as radio cards.\n\nFor: teams who want it to feel like a serious, familiar tool (Linear / Stripe territory).\nTradeoff: the safest choice — it will look like a lot of other software." },
    { "id": "note-nightshift", "page": "page-redesign", "x": 3080, "y": 1180, "w": 340, "text": "NIGHTSHIFT — dark, glowing\n\nSpace Grotesk + DM Sans · near-black · violet→cyan gradient accent · glass cards · one huge price hero.\n\nFor: a brand that wants to feel premium and different; great on marketing pages.\nTradeoff: dark UIs are harder for long daily use and for printing/label previews; needs a light mode eventually." },
    { "id": "note-sunny", "page": "page-redesign", "x": 3080, "y": 2360, "w": 340, "text": "SUNNY — warm, playful\n\nSora + Nunito · cream · coral + teal + yellow · big radii · 2px outlines with offset shadows · sticker badges (\"Cheapest!\") · stepper on Ship.\n\nFor: small sellers who find carrier sites intimidating — friendly, obvious, fun.\nTradeoff: dense screens (batch, reports) need a calmer variant of the same system." },
    { "id": "note-product", "page": "page-product", "x": 1560, "y": -150, "w": 420, "text": "v1 · Bold editorial (Direction C) — what is built and live today. Kept for reference; superseded once a redesign direction is picked." },
    { "id": "note-system", "page": "page-system", "x": 0, "y": -130, "w": 420, "text": "System design · read 1 → 7\n\nArchitecture, then the data it stores, the API on top, and the three flows that carry money or state: buying a label, tracking, pay-as-you-go billing on Stripe. EasyPost is the single shipping provider — rates, labels, refunds, trackers, address verification — behind a thin interface (7), so nothing else in the system knows about it. Unaffected by the visual redesign." }
  ],
  "launch": { "view": "canvas", "page": "page-redesign" }
